WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.3 · Financial Management
Project budgets, cost allocation and full cost recovery

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A project’s true cost includes its fair share of the costs that keep you running.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. List direct costs: quantity times unit cost.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Allocate shared costs with one written basis.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Name the costs unpaid help is covering.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Pan del Barrio (Social enterprise · company, Peru)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Pan del Barrio: apprenticeship direct costs US$22,130, plus US$4,550 shared; about US$2,223 per trainee. Employer fees cover 56%.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create one full-cost project budget.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
